acme_infra: Hey team — rerank API started returning 400s for our nightly batch. Happens for all jobs since ~04:12 UTC. curl output below:

acme_infra: ```bash
curl -s -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/rerank -H 'Authorization: Bearer sk_****' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d @payload.json
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
{ \"error\": \"Invalid request\", \"detail\": \"schema error: expected top-level 'items' array but found 'requests'\" }
```

support_ana: thanks — can you paste the exact payload.json you sent (no creds)?

acme_infra: sure, pasted below (we wrap everything in a top-level envelope with metadata):

acme_infra: ```json
{
  "job_id": "nightly-2026-03-17",
  "env": "prod",
  "payload": {
    "requests": [
      {
        "top_k": "2",
        "candidates": [
          { "content": "Answer A", "score": 0.7 },
          { "content": "Answer B", "score": 0.5 }
        ]
      },
      {
        "top_k": -1,
        "candidates": null
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

support_ana: OK — I see a few red flags: 1) API expects an 'items' array at the top level (not payload.requests), 2) candidate objects should use 'text' and optional 'id' fields (not 'content'), 3) top_k should be an integer > 0 (your second request has -1), and 4) candidates must be a non-empty array (not null). Any chance this job runner changed recently?

engineer_liam: tagging in. For rerank we intentionally tightened schema validation in the last deploy (reject unknown envelopes) to avoid ambiguous routing. That means we no longer silently accept nested payload.requests. The error message is coming from the schema validator: \"expected top-level 'items' array but found 'requests'\".

engineer_liam: quick repro steps: take their JSON, transform payload.requests -> items, canonicalize candidate objects to {\"id\": \"opt-1\", \"text\": \"Answer A\"}, and ensure top_k is numeric (not string). With that change the endpoint returns 200. Example good payload below.

engineer_liam: ```json
{
  "items": [
    {
      "top_k": 2,
      "candidates": [
        { "id": "c1", "text": "Answer A" },
        { "id": "c2", "text": "Answer B" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

cs_rohan: is this a regression for other customers or only them?

engineer_liam: the validator change shipped in the last minor (2026-03-16) and should only affect clients that relied on permissive envelope handling. Most clients were already sending top-level items. We rolled a short note to integrations but missed a few offline clients.

support_ana: workaround for them: 1) patch the job runner to map payload.requests -> items and content->text, coerce top_k to int and skip null/empty candidates; or 2) if they can't patch immediately, we can proxy transform their requests on our side for a short window. Which do you prefer?

acme_infra: we can patch the runner but it's slow to deploy across 30 workers. Could you enable a temporary transform on your side for the next 6 hours? We'll push the patch during that window.

engineer_liam: we can enable a small proxy rule to accept the envelope and rewrite to the canonical format. I'll coordinate with infra. deploy-bot: please queue a small config toggle for support proxying for org acme_infra, ttl 6h.

deploy-bot: @engineer_liam — request accepted. Proxy toggle queued on canary, will apply in ~6 mins and emit logs to #eng-runtime.

support_ana: added a short repro/KB entry to the ticket: transform envelope.requests -> items, candidate.content -> text, ensure top_k positive integer, candidates non-empty array. I'll follow up when proxy is live. :thumbsup:

acme_infra: huge thanks. Appreciate the quick turnaround. We'll confirm once nightly job succeeds.

support_ana: noted — logging this as high_priority for the next 6 hours and following up to close the ticket after their patch.

acme_infra: confirmed 05:05 UTC — job cleared after your proxy went live. No more 400s. We'll roll the runner patch later today. Thanks everyone! :tada:
